{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization","id":797033,"title":"Open Dev Two: Compacts and Globalization","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-30T15:10:30-08:00","id":797033,"title":"Open Dev Two: Compacts and Globalization","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-2e-open-dev-tier-two-compacts-and-globalization/\" target=\"_blank\">New blogpost means we need a new thread. </a>Expect my response soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-30-2015, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T15:32:04-08:00","id":797047,"title":"","content":"Let's not have this thread devolve into us crossposting our comments.<br /> <br /> I'll start off by saying that I'm ecstatic Vigil 2e is going with such a global view of things, and it'll be really fun to have a whole host of international flashpoints for us to drool over. After all, there are monsters wherever there are people, and people are everywhere.<br /> <br /> It'll be really fun to see what Compacts people end up listing as their favorites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T15:46:23-08:00","id":797053,"title":"","content":"Looking forward to seeing everyones thoughts and getting into it all over again. This OpenDev process has been really enlightening and engaging; I don't think I've had this much passionate debate about sides, factions and interpretations, since we all got voting on Dark Eras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T15:53:19-08:00","id":797054,"title":"","content":"So for the core point, gloablising Compacts.<br /> <br /> <br /> To me, I think that saying here's what the Swedish Branch of the Long Night looks like, and creating an entirely separate Protestant faith based Compact that only exists in Sweden and fills the same thematic niche are equally good.<br /> <br /> So basically, I wouldn't sweat too much if a Compact feels very geographically localised and I certainly wouldn't want Compacts redesigned to make them more global. In that case I think a separate organisation would be superior to diluting a Compact.<br /> <br /> Network Zero is definitely global and I'm just as interested to hear how the USA and South Korean members interact as I am to hear about the South Korean members. The Union is so specific that there's probably entirely separate organisations filling it's niche of &quot;Average Joes protecting their community&quot; for different parts of America. Forget the Union in London, I want to know what the Union in inner city Baltimore is like. (Assuming the Ascending Ones aren't around for some reason).<br /> <br /> <br /> One thing I've always wanted is for each Hunter Compact and Conspiracy to start with a couple of paragraphs explicitly stating it's Theme. I think that would help quite a lot for globalisation.<br /> <br /> Once you see that the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood's theme is &quot;diplomatic academic occultists defending the university and students&quot;* written down like that it really gets the creative juices flowing.<br /> <br /> Just looking at that I'm already imagining their English equivalent as an ancient Oxbridge drinking society, with kooky traditions, outdated attitudes, and a more freemasonic flavour to their occultism instead of the neopagan vibe I get from the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood.<br /> <br /> <br /> *I'm torn between saying this is the MBS' theme, or that they have two complimentary themes.<br /> <br /> <b>What are your top 3 favorite existing compacts and why?</b><ul><li>Null Mysteriis - I like the fact their goal is non-violent, and I like the science angle. I hope in 2E they're less likely to jump to pesudoscientific theories and more wordcount is given to Science-as-a-methodology</li> <li>Maiden's Blood Sisterhood - The diplomatic and intellectual approach appeals to me, but really I just want to play the charachter in their sample artwork (with some minor magical abilities, not enough to qualify as non-human in any meaningful sense - something like Second Sight's Thamaturges)</li> <li>Ama San - It's bursting with good ideas; but I'd say the bit that really does it for me is the fact their power comes from growing up together in a genuinely supportive environment, with underwater hunting coming second. I really hope the roles will get updated from the draft I saw though.</li> </ul><br /> <b>What are your thoughts on globalization and locations for the compacts you selected?</b><br /> <br /> I think that Null Mysteriis are already global. They're founded in London, but Paris is mentioned and they show up in the Philadelphia appendix. I'm fine with this, the real life scientific community has strong global links, and it makes sense that NM would be a singular organisation with a worldwide membership.<br /> <br /> The Maiden's Blood Sisterhood - I think I'd rather keep them as unique to one location. As compacts go, they feel small and intimate and I think that should stay. I would like to see groups who share themes with the MBS around the world, but from an in charachter perspective they're unrelated groups.<br /> <br /> Ama San - Ignoring the fact they're an Edo era compact; I genuinely think they can't work as a globalised group. MBS feel small and intimate; the Ama San are built entirely around the concept. If you don't know all the other Hunters from birth, it's not the Ama San. But small villages defined by a close relationship to the supernatural can work anywhere, consider Wall from Neil Gaimen's Stardust as another example. It's nothing like the Ama San, and yet it really is another manifestation of that same theme.<br /> <br /> <b>How married are you to the history of the compacts?</b><br /> <br /> Is the unwritten implication of this question &quot;what do you feel about rewriting the history to make a group more globalised?&quot;.<br /> <br /> If it is I'd be against that. I'd rather new groups are introduced as separate manifestations of the theme. However I'm fine with touching up a compact if it makes them even better at being their 1E self.<br /> <br /> For example I wouldn't to see the MBS rewritten to justify them as a more global organisation, but touching up their history to give them a bit more occultism in their DNA; a splash of neo-paganism, a bit more room for minor supernatural abilities like Thamaturges. I'd love that.<br /> <br /> <b>We have compacts formed around</b><br /> <br /> A new theme? Without a doubt <i>Exploration</i>! The WoD has some lovely otherworlds and a Compact based around exploring one of them (my suspension of disbelief would start to crack if a Compact was active in multiple other worlds and I do think Exploration fits better at Tier 2 than 3) would be awesome.<br /> <br /> My preference would be exploring the Underworld, because it's the one where the laws of physics are the closest to normal, it has a lot of relevance to mundane life, and interesting places to visit.<br /> <br /> The obvious location would be Paris, because of the catacombs. Naturally different groups with different otherworlds to explore could exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-30-2015, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T16:13:46-08:00","id":797064,"title":"","content":"The globalization question brings us a funny dichotomy; do we want Compacts to be archetypes that can be customized to fit various places, or do we want deep, specific Compacts intrinsically tied to a particular place and history?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T16:33:54-08:00","id":797072,"title":"","content":"I believe applying a global view on the Vigil requires a very measured approach, due to a certain feature of the setting: While it varies from Compact to Compact (and Conspiracy to Conspiracy), these organizations straddle the line between being actual entities with their own history, and being iconic examples of their type. The Union, for instance, has a historical background that is mostly secondary to their core theme - communities banding together against common threats. Their history is vague enough to allow greater flexibility, but as a trade-off they are less of an living organization and more of a template. Groups like it would crop up in multiple places but calling them by the same name would be off-putting and inelegant, even within the same country. I'm thinking over making a certain split enforced mainly by the layout of the book: Firstly, The Union described not as an organization, but as a certain template and then, for example, the &quot;Rust-belt Grapevine&quot; as a specific group with it's own history, which may or may not be on good terms (or even know about) with their Union-y counterparts.<br /> <br /> From another angle, there is this: The way the game-line is designed, every Compact also has a monopoly on a certain method to the Vigil, which can feed into the following problem: A possible pitfall of expanding the Compacts abroad is giving the impression they are all there is to the Vigil, instead of just being examples of Hunter organizations. \u200bThe text would have to underscore how many and varied Hunter Compacts are. The Stereotypes sections are somewhat at fault (it's more of an observation than an actual complaint), since they only mention the other known groups. Clearly, that's what a Stereotype section is meant to do, but it helps forget that the is more to CofD-World than just what's written up. Also, since globalization is a relatively new phenomenon, multiple Compacts would have developed in greater isolation. With the advent of globalization, any expanding Compacts would likely come across their local counterparts, with varying results. I believe that the text and its layout need to help delineate between Compacts and Conspiracies as templates and as specific organizations. It would be greatly helped by including build-your-own-Compact tools.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T16:37:05-08:00","id":797075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=797054#post797054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Union is so specific that there's probably entirely separate organisations filling it's niche of &quot;Average Joes protecting their community&quot; for different parts of America. Forget the Union in London, I want to know what the Union in inner city Baltimore is like. (Assuming the Ascending Ones aren't around for some reason).</div> </div> </div> </div>I just wanted to say something about this. I worked with unions in Baltimore for years and talked about the &quot;the Union&quot; Compact with a fellow organizer and how it would look in Baltimore. We both kind of laughed about it. Reading through the Compact history it tries to build some sort of network between the different unions in the U.S. which is there to an extent, but there is also a lot of bad blood. In Baltimore alone remnants of the vicious split between SEIU and UNITE HERE still present in local union politics not to mention numerous company unions working against more radical unions. In this country this story is played out in almost every city to varying degrees with battle lines being drawn over organizing strategies, membership, and power. For my friend and me, this left us thinking what Union is this supposed to be because there are definitely some we know that would be just as willing to work with monsters. We ended thinking that it would be better to make a specific Union that organized intensely, but also trained its members in combat and forced them to look after their neighbors.<br /> <br /> My point of bringing this up is not to just focus on the problems in the Union's development, but to point out how a single Compact can be hurt by being too inclusive towards their &quot;theme&quot;. That being said I think certain Compacts definitely work better with vague theoretical boundaries (Network Zero). On the question about globalization, I don't know if the answer is to find a way to rewrite Compacts that already exist that don't work everywhere to all of a sudden work internationally. Perhaps working off of the question about themes the focus of globalizing Compacts should be on developing Compacts in other nations that willingly work together because their themes align enough. For The Union, you could have a Compact in South Africa based off the Shack Dwellers Movement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T16:43:50-08:00","id":797076,"title":"","content":"This idea of globalizing Compacts could possibly lead to another way of differentiating them from Conspiracies beyond just being smaller in that they are also more willing to work with other groups. They could be shown as being more aware of their lack of power and knowledge and in turn build bonds easier whereas Conspiracies are too entrenched in their efforts to see anyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T18:19:01-08:00","id":797115,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I guess compacts are going to get larger.<br /> <br /> Or at least I don't see much point in globalizing a group that only consists of 50 people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T18:21:16-08:00","id":797117,"title":"","content":"<ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">What are your top 3 favorite existing compacts and why? These can be pulled from any book that\u2019s been published thus far, including compacts that are no longer around.</span><ul><li>The Union, first and foremost. I strongly sympathise with its straightforward ideas. No secret agendas, no conspiracies, just genuine good intentions. Sure, they have a dark side, like everything else in the CofD, but they are flaws I enjoy as a player and storyteller.</li> <li>The Maiden's Blood Sisterhood is amazing. I only learnt of it today looking for the full list of Compacts (I needed a third choice), but I just love it for how progressive it is. I can already imagine a bunch of different concepts for it.</li> <li>Network Zero. Another group with idealistic, straightforward good intentions. Again, they have flaws, but I'm okay with that.</li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">What are your thoughts on globalization and locations for the compacts you selected?</span><ul><li>The Union can <i>easily</i> be expanded to Latin America via the history of workers' movements throughout it. From Argentina's Peron presidencies to Brazil's Landless Workers, etc.</li> <li>The Maiden's Blood Sisterhood's core concept (women banding together to defend themselves from the predators) can easily exist in different countries throughout the world, especially if the Compact doesn't do a diaspora, but instead the same concept pops up in different parts of the world and then they come in contact and share info and resources.</li> <li>The article already covered Network Zero.</li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">How married are you to the history of the compacts? Have those details come up in actual play for your group?</span><ul><li>Don't really follow official fluff unless I absolutely love it. I tend to treat history as a suggestion at best. :P</li> <li>Nope, not for any of them.</li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">We have compacts formed around playing styles such as belief, hedonism, research, atonement, communication, defense, vengeance, hunting specific monster types such as vampires, etc. If you had your pick of \u201ca\u201d new style of play that\u2019d be fun to play, what would be the theme and why? Where would it be based? Please try to avoid creating/naming new compacts, as I do want to reserve that honor for my future team.</span><ul><li>Really want to see a compact like the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood, but dedicated to LGBT people. There are thematic parallels that can be made between the Hunter existence and being part of a gender or sexual minority. Secret-keeping, facing the idea that your loved ones might not understand you, the relief of finding someone you can share experiences with, and so on.</li> <li>The theme could be &quot;support&quot;. The new Compact could support individual cells regardless of how they choose to go about the hunt, whether they take up arms and kill predators, or they just gather intel, or they try to negotiate. The group, since it has had to accommodate all sorts of diverse identities with not a lot in common, would have learnt by now to articulate its strength as a facilitator and mediator, with the flaw that it obviously lacks focus and isn't terribly good at any one aspect of the Hunt.</li> <li>The group could be based on San Francisco, to get the obvious location out of the way; or perhaps more interestingly, Greenwich Village (where the Stonewall Riots took place). Basing it on New York City would serve to reinforce the Compact's plurality and eclecticness, since NYC boasts a great deal of cultural diversity.</li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T20:04:18-08:00","id":797157,"title":"","content":"I know Mortail Remains had something of a mixed reception, but I adored both Habibti Ma and Utopia Now; the former is distressingly relevant still, and the latter has a lot of really fun potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T20:05:36-08:00","id":797158,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if my comment got eaten, or if they were just so long they are taking longer to load, so I'm including them here. I really like the Korea idea that Monica talked about for Network Zero and think that will add a very interesting aspect to the game. <br /> <br /> Does the yet unrevealed First Nations Compact I commissioned for Dark Eras count? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Of what we know -<br /> <br /> <b>1. Favourite Compacts</b><br /> <u>a) Ahl Al-Jabal</u> - My GF is Ismaili and I have a degree in Islamic History, so this one is close to my heart in many ways. Ahl Al-Jabal is freaking perfect. It nails Ismaili beliefs and traditions, is a positive, anti-terrorist Muslim group, and get's the history of Nizari State pretty much spot on, which is rare thanks to the hashashin myths. Ismailis also have large presence in my home of Calgary, our mayor is one, and many of my friends from high school are too. <br /> <br /> <u>b) Bear Lodge</u> - Another compact that is local for me and can be found in a lot of the areas I lived in as a kid. <br /> <br /> c) Third spot is a bit tougher, but I'm rather fond of <u>Utopia Now</u>. They have a neat way of interpreting GM Angels and Demons, plus they have a sweet Bioshock aesthetic going. <br /> <br /> <b>2. Globalization and location </b>- Before I start this, I'd like to be on record as loving the idea of Network Zero having a South Korean dimension. I think that's a logical progression, and it adds new territory to the map of CofD. Great job! I've tried to take some inspiration from that and continue on with my own thoughts below. <br /> <br /> a) Ahl Al-Jabal is pretty easy to globalize, to the point that if globalization of Hunter 2e is a goal, i think it should automatically be included as a compact. They exist anywhere that there is a significant population of Ismailis, which means you could find them anywhere in the Middle East, Asia proper, North America, Europe, or Africa. In particular, Dubai, Dar Es-Salam, Syria, Northern India/Pakistan, and Calgary come to my mind as locations that could be used in conjunction with the Ahl Al-Jabal for the Slasher Chronicles. I'd also imagine that they'd have moved into former Soviet territories such as Tajikistan in the last 20-25 years. <br /> <br /> b) Not as much globalization here, although perhaps there have been some attempts restore relations with the Russian Federation by setting up Bear Lodges in Siberia? There could be a somewhat friendly competition between the Asian and North American chapters. An African &quot;Big Game/Safari&quot; chapter is another possibility, although that runs the risk of overlap with the Ashwood Abbey. Then again, that could lead to some not so friendly competition. <br /> <br /> c) Utopia Now has an interesting way of globalizing. They were originally based out of San Fran and want to build their paradise city in the middle of the Pacific. What if they became kind of a reverse Pacific Rim, seeding chapters all throughout the Pacific nations. Obviously, they would be drawn to places like Tokyo, Sydney, Hong Kong, and Seoul to find Institutional Demons, but what if they went for older angels as well? Things hiding in the volcanos and the ruins? If someone gets a beed on an institutional demon hiding in Ankor Wat, that would draw Utopia now like flies, so I could see them filling positions in Singapore, Thailand, Cambodia, Vietnam, Brunei and Indonesia just as easily. After all, Utopia Now is a start up, but in an increasing globalized and connected world, even a start up can have an international presence. Finally, and I think this is the neat part, Utopia Now seems like a logical compact to touch an area that hasn't been in any CofD product so far: Oceania. Fiji, Tonga, Samoa and the other Polynesian Islands are basically virgin territory that could have some interesting aspect to explore. I think there's a neat opportunity for overlap here.<br /> <br /> <b>3. History</b> - I'm a continuity nerd, so in general I'd prefer to see an expansion of past history rather than a rewriting. For Ahl Al-Jabal, please don't touch the history we've been given. It was expertly crafted. Rather, summarize it, then tell us what happened to the compact after they got kicked out of Persia by the Mongols. For the Bear Lodge and Utopia Now, I'm less tied to it.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>New Play Styles </b>- I'll add my vote for a diplomatic/political compact. That's an area the game is lacking in, and I could totally see a compact trying to pull a Bismark on monsters, negotiating them so they attack each other instead of the humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T20:30:28-08:00","id":797164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=797157#post797157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know Mortail Remains had something of a mixed reception, but I adored both Habibti Ma and Utopia Now; the former is distressingly relevant still, and the latter has a lot of really fun potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I could pick four, Habibti Ma would have been my fourth. Not the Egypt as it was that we all learn about, but Egypt as it is today, a Muslim country that is still in revolution. Super relevant in terms of theme, targets supernaturals through their cults, which gives them a unique focus. If we start to globalize, they could be found all along North Africa, East Africa (via the Nile), the Greater Middle East (lots of Egyptians travel for business, I knew many in Abu Dhabi), plus small cliques in Europe and NA. Plus, they can fight pretty much anything besides Prommies and maybe Beasts. One of the best compacts bar none, and definitely worthy of a spot in the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 12-31-2015, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T20:37:04-08:00","id":797167,"title":"","content":"Second Chances, it's cruel of you to tease that Dark Eras content! Your expansion doubled my interest in Doubting Souls.<br /> <br /> I adore the idea of Utopia Now branching out through the Pacific and into Asia; I especially enjoy the threat of buyout by a Chinese millionaire and the ensuing moral crisis in the group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T20:45:17-08:00","id":797170,"title":"","content":"D<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=797167#post797167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I adore the idea of Utopia Now branching out through the Pacific and into Asia; I especially enjoy the threat of buyout by a Chinese millionaire and the ensuing moral crisis in the group.</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <br /> If I make it through open call, I'm going to find a way to make this canon. Awesome idea!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T21:39:20-08:00","id":797183,"title":"","content":"damn it! I missed making a thread for the new blog post! Oh well- I'll make a post about the subject after I'll get back home from the University :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T21:49:38-08:00","id":797190,"title":"","content":"Oo! Oo! I just had another idea for the Bear Lodge. Canada's pretty close to the US culturally, unless you go to the parts of my country that aren't actually close to the States. Go to the North West Territories and Nunavut, linking the Bear Lodge to the Inuit and the Northern First Nations. Iqaluit Would be an awesome city to focus on. It's just short of having to deal with the Midnight Sun, so there is still night all year around, but that creates a very short night (2 hours) for Vampires in the summer, and a very long night (22 hours) for Hunters in the day. Spirits would also likely trend to the extremes, which could be a pain in the ass for Hunters and Werewolves alike. From there, you are also a hope, skip and jump away from Greenland, which deserves more love too, and has at least one canonical Mummy cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T00:40:23-08:00","id":797222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=797064#post797064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The globalization question brings us a funny dichotomy; do we want Compacts to be archetypes that can be customized to fit various places, or do we want deep, specific Compacts intrinsically tied to a particular place and history?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd definately say deep specific Compacts.<br /> <br /> However I don't think it's an exclusive choice. You could probably have the archetype in a sentence or so &quot;Average joes protecting their community&quot; with the rest of the text being one or more deep compacts that serve as an example of that archetype<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=797075#post797075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wanted to say something about this. I worked with unions in Baltimore</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay, someone who can answer my curiositiy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Would The Union as written in 1E likely have any presence in the same part of Baltimore where you'd find Avon Barksdale and his ilk from The Wire?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=797117#post797117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The theme could be &quot;support&quot;. The new Compact could support individual cells regardless of how they choose to go about the hunt</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually how the Union does things; perhaps this is not suprising. The Union is written as a group who's goal is to &quot;defend my community&quot;; which is exactly what you're proposing - just with their community being the LGBT community.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T04:18:34-08:00","id":797271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=797064#post797064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The globalization question brings us a funny dichotomy; do we want Compacts to be archetypes that can be customized to fit various places, or do we want deep, specific Compacts intrinsically tied to a particular place and history?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you cut to the point there. I'd tend to come down on the archetype side because due to space constraints you don't actually get an all that deep picture of the C&amp;Cs. I find it also makes the Hunter setting feel rather small.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T04:56:23-08:00","id":797276,"title":"","content":"Mine comment repost.<ul><li><b>What are your top 3 favorite existing compacts and why?</b></li> </ul>I love all from 1ED corebook, but my Top 3 Favorites:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Null Mysteriis</b> \u2013 it\u2019s very refreshing to play scientist trying to explain supernatural in NATURAL ways. Just make their theories sound more scientific like, less like from pulp magazines.</li> <li><b>Network Zero</b> \u2013 monster watching YouTubers are fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also, they make great \u201cMasquerade\u201d breach plot devices when confronted with &quot;monsters&quot;.</li> <li><b>Ashwood Abbey</b> \u2013 hedonistic society treating the Vigil as great hobby and being true to themselves that hunting is FUN. Also, love Hellfire Club vibe of them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ol>( As we are at proper forum - I also love Loyalists and Long Night, only think the Union is to &quot;neuter&quot; - maybe because it's only USA group. But if Union would be remade as I advice - see below - it could be very interesting to play. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<ul><li><b>What are your thoughts on globalization and locations for the compacts you selected?</b></li> </ul>I think Compacts SHOULD be \u201cglobal, but individual\u201d \u2013 they should be network of chapter houses, ranging from one country\u2019s region ( and only one chapter house then ) to whole world. They would be \u201calliances\u201d of similar organisations \u2013 each chapter house can has other local name, local rules variant but in the end, they work under very similar general ethos. There is one \u201cUnion\u201d, made by various local, smaller \u201cunions\u201d that go from the same blue collar sort, but from different time period \u2013 each chapter house can be a small regional organisation in their own rank. But they still answer collectively as \u201cUnion\u201d in general hunters culture. Or each Long Nights\u2019 \u201ccongregasion\u201d is in the end different protestant small church \u2013 they are only connected on the idea of Apocalypse coming and need to redeem some monsters. Or each chapter house of Ashwood Abbey it\u2019s Hellfire Club with it\u2019s own rituals and history, maybe even local name \u2013 still, they are all nominal under rule ship of Scotland HQ.<ul><li><b>How married are you to the history of the compacts? Have those details come up in actual play for your group?</b></li> </ul>Not very much, but some vague history of the group \u2013 or how it\u2019s spread on the world \u2013 can lead to some general story ideas to be used in chronicle.<ul><li><b>If you had your pick of \u201ca\u201d new style of play that\u2019d be fun to play, what would be the theme and why?</b></li> </ul>Interesting could be group based on the \u201csearching of missing persons\u201d \u2013 this group was very much missing in 1ED. Other group could be made about \u201cdiplomacy\u201d between supernatural, and making \u201cPax Romana\u201d \u2013 but I feel it should be more in Conspiracy territory. ( Fan created Lords Stewardes were great way of showing this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-09-2016, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T05:19:32-08:00","id":797288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=797222#post797222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yay, someone who can answer my curiositiy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Would The Union as written in 1E likely have any presence in the same part of Baltimore where you'd find Avon Barksdale and his ilk from The Wire?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is a pretty interesting question. Just as a side note to give you some perspective on unions and The WIre, the chief of security at one union hotel new David Simon from his crime reporting days and was inspiration for Bunk, Major Colvin (the guy who made Hamsterdam), and personally arrested the people who inspired Barksdale.<br /> <br /> Now to answer your question I think you have to answer one question I still had from the 1E about the Union. Do they still organize businesses and see that as a way to increase power and safety? I think how they are written now makes them more out to be pretty diverse group of people protecting their community. These are two different things. I think if you go with the first route then you can have some pretty interesting answers to your question. Every union local for the most part has a union hall, this building can be away from the neighborhoods of its members or towards it. Its members tend to live in neighborhoods that exist away from the hubs of their jobs (hotels, casinos, construction, hospitals, etc.). Organizers and volunteers will go into these neighborhoods for numerous reasons, but their focus normally is on making either the entire city better or there specific work sector better.<br /> <br /> In Baltimore, it is very likely that you live in the west side or the east side and work downtown and belong to a union that operates there. So you could be a member of the Union and its activities while also living in a neighborhood likes Barksdale's. The Ascending Ones or Night Watch might be more prominent in your neighborhood and do things you question. How do you as a Hunter reconcile what then is happening in your community while you possibly fight somewhere else? Can you effect change in other areas to better protect your row? I think these are the questions that are more realistic for a Compact based on union. I hope that answers your question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T05:38:05-08:00","id":797291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=797271#post797271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you cut to the point there. I'd tend to come down on the archetype side because due to space constraints you don't actually get an all that deep picture of the C&amp;Cs. I find it also makes the Hunter setting feel rather small.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me it's archetypes that make the setting feel small, because they end up being treated as specific groups anyway, and very dilute ones as a result. I'd prefer to start with specific groups and root them in the context of their locations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T05:52:14-08:00","id":797296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> because they end up being treated as specific groups anyway, </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. Though, I think the CofD have gotten better at it as things have gone along there's often a tendency to go back to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T06:19:07-08:00","id":797305,"title":"","content":"Interesting stuff Iladas.<br /> <br /> One thing that springs to mind is that Night Watch and The Union are probably both manifestations of the same archetype: defending my community. But that doens't mean they have to agree with each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=797291#post797291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me it's archetypes that make the setting feel small, because they end up being treated as specific groups anyway, and very dilute ones as a result. I'd prefer to start with specific groups and root them in the context of their locations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T06:27:16-08:00","id":797309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=797305#post797305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing that springs to mind is that Night Watch and The Union are probably both manifestations of the same archetype: defending my community. But that doens't mean they have to agree with each other.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Saying that gets me thinking that each Compact is broken up into two themes: why they hunt and how they hunt. From there local alliances can be developed. It would be interesting for the developers to think about including ways and mechanics that would streamline how to develop local (international?) Vigil politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T06:37:47-08:00","id":797315,"title":"","content":"I'm also all in for separating Tier of play from Compacts and Conspiracies. To use most <b>Hunter </b>appropriate media inspirations - <b>The X Files </b>are chronicle about VASCU cell on Tier 1, without all backing up or Teleinformatics powers. In meanwhile <b>Supernatural</b> is non-organisation play from Tier 1 to Tier 3 and back again, in that Winchesters save single people, then rescue a one state and then save whole world - all without rally joining any Compact or Conspiracy. ( Well, there was Roadhouse in season 2, but it was still more &quot;we are only meeting some hunters from it - we are not part of that crew. )<br /> <br /> I say that we should separate Tier of play from structure of organisation. All Compact and Conspiracies can be split in to those groups ( from the bottom ) that have geographical jurisdictions:<br /> 1. Cell - Town, city's district.<br /> 2. Chapter House ( Division?) - Region, small country, state in Americas.<br /> 3. Headquarters (HQ) - Whole globe.<br /> <br /> And with this partition we easily can have Compacts that are based on Chapter Houses from whole the world. each slightly different and with local variation, maybe even it's own name - but still answering as one Compacts name. We can have one &quot;Union&quot;, that is divide in to lesser Chapter Houses ( various &quot;unions&quot;), each with it's own agenda in the bigger creed of Compact, leaders and even names. Our Chapter Houses may even fight between themselves. Or that we can various &quot;congregation&quot; of Long Night, each being different church in reality. Compacts still can have one HQ, but it's center of the group only in name - each Chapter House is in reality independent. Each &quot;Ashwood Abbey&quot; Chapter House is, in reality, different Hellfire Club, with it's own name, policies, leaders. First Chapter is more the model to repeat or embody than direct commander.<br /> <br /> Conspiracies, then, are groups with direct chain of command. HQ is sending orders, you must to obey them. Chapter Houses can still fight, but central make sure it's not all out conflict and in the end - you are agent to the same force, not similar like in Compacts.<br /> <br /> It's nicely sum up mine idea - Chapter Houses in Compact are<i> loosely similar </i>( and could be name differently ), Chapters in Conspiracy are the <i>same</i>, in the end.<br /> <br /> And yes, in this model, Loyalists of Thule becomes Conspiracy, because of the power Three Man of Munich on the rest of members. Probably Ascending Ones, as so loose, various cults, become then Compact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-31-2015, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T06:40:07-08:00","id":797317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=797222#post797222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's actually how the Union does things; perhaps this is not suprising. The Union is written as a group who's goal is to &quot;defend my community&quot;; which is exactly what you're proposing - just with their community being the LGBT community.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, not really. The Union is not non-judgmental; that's one of its flaws (and this is okay). From what we got in Compacts and Conspiracies, the Union tends to be militant and confrontative about things. Their factions only get more and more radical and extremist, rather than offer alternatives to violence (there's no diplomatic or research-oriented faction, for example). So no, the Union is not what I was suggesting.<br /> <br /> Second of all, if each concept precluded anything remotely similar, we wouldn't have the Night Watch or the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood, which are different and unique takes on the idea of defending a community. There's still plenty of room for that concept to be explored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T07:13:10-08:00","id":797335,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">reposting from the blog<br /> <br /> 1) my 3 favorite groups? well, let\u2019s see..</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2013 Ashwood Abbey: I like those bastards, I really do. Their desire for freedom and pleasure and the way they channel all of humanity\u2019s vices into the Vigil is truly alluring for me. I always like playing such unstable characters, making them into a wild card at any situation.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2013 Keepers of the Source: yeah, I know some people don\u2019t like them because their philosophy is not supported by what Mage says- but I\u2019m not playing Mage. Anyway, I like their connection to Ley Lines and other \u201cplaces of power\u201d and that they seek to protect them from being manipulated by witches and similar beings. The fact that they don\u2019t agree with Mages about how magic works only makes me like them better.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2013 Scarlet Watch: not even out and I already like them! (once that place belonged to the Promethean Brotherhood, but they are already half conspiracy so I don\u2019t feel bad with it :P). Anyway, for me the Watch feels like the \u201cHeritage House done right\u201d- their emphasis on the old families who are bound by blood and fate to carry on the Vigil and their rich merchants origin done wrong by vampires and the Church makes me eager to play one as soon as possible! (also, on my table, they are still around- maybe as a compact and maybe they reclaimed their lost rites. Still didn\u2019t decided).</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">2)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Well, among the three the Ashwood Abbey are the easiest as far as globalization is concerned- Compacts and Conspiracies has already presented them as having chapters all around the world, all tied together by the licenses of the pyramid scheme. While each chapter may have its own view on a \u201cgood game\u201d, the way their structure works well to keep them working together all across the world.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Keepers of the Source, however, feel a lot more localized- while there should be similar groups all around the world (Chinese geomancers for example) and the Keepers does seem to have an interest to spread in order to protect more places from being abused, I\u2019m not sure they have enough resources to do so. If they go for globalization, I assume they\u2019ll work as some sort of \u201coccult Greenpeace\u201d as a green movement with small chapters around the world, all desperate for funding. The other option would be tying them specifically to San Francisco in order to strength their hold over the city- although as idealists, I think they\u2019ll choose the first option.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Now, the Scarlet Watch, if they are still around, seem to be a former conspiracy- so I assume that they may have some connections both in Latin Europe and the North America. Assuming that their families are still rich enough (and willing to actually invest that money in the Vigil), they may still be able to operate on both continents, even if not as much as they want to. The same is true for Salem, although I feel their connections to Europe are a lot less strong during that Era.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">3) new edition usually means some changes for the history of the groups. Usually the backstory of certain compact or conspiracy doesn\u2019t play a big role in my games, and it is used mostly for thinking about a Chronicle size plot hooks or when developing the setting (that is, it stays on the background, but still influence the game).</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">4) well, what I would really want to see is a \u201cmostly male group\u201d who have a reason to not include women in the compact which is not Chauvinism. Yeah, I understand why there should be female-only groups and I like them, but I really feel an urge to see a male exclusive one. That was one of the reasons I was excited for getting the Bijin in Edo Era before discovering that the initial \u201cmale escorts compact\u201d idea was abandoned to the level there wasn\u2019t even an example character of such concept in the draft. Also a group of Ghosts Hunters would be nice.</span></span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 12-31-2015, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T08:00:13-08:00","id":797350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=797309#post797309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying that gets me thinking that each Compact is broken up into two themes: why they hunt and how they hunt. From there local alliances can be developed. It would be interesting for the developers to think about including ways and mechanics that would streamline how to develop local (international?) Vigil politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually say there's three themes. How we Hunt, Why we Hunt, and Who we Are.<br /> <br /> But not all Compacts Have all three.<br /> <br /> The Maiden's Blood Sisterhood for example has all three:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">How we hunt: Accademic investigation, diplomacy, perhaps a splash of occultism.<br /> Why we hunt: To protect the student community.<br /> Who we are: Feminists / Students and University staff</div> <br /> But Null Mysteriis only really does Why We Hunt.<br /> Ashwood Abbey does Why we Hunt and Who we Are, but it doesn't do How we Hunt.<br /> The Talbot Group does Why we Hunt and How we Hunt, but not Who we are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=797317#post797317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second of all, if each concept precluded anything remotely similar, we wouldn't have the Night Watch or the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood, which are different and unique takes on the idea of defending a community. There's still plenty of room for that concept to be explored.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that's what I was thinking of when I made the comparason. I mean, The Union might be written with xenophobia as their flaw - but in 2E talks about regional differences that doesn't have to apply to every location. In fact it would kind of miss the point if it did.<br /> <br /> Like the Union your proposed group are community defenders and they support individual cells regardless of how they choose to go about the hunt; supporting individual cells like that is the core of the Union.<br /> <br /> You bring up Night Watch, and Maiden's Blood Sisterhood. And well, why not? Lets call the archetype &quot;Community Defenders&quot;. Why not say that The Union are the Community Defenders of a largish wash of rust belt and small town USA. Night Watch are the community defenders of west side and east side Baltimore. Your group are the Community Defenders of various gay neighbourhoods. The Maiden's Blood Sisterhood...<br /> <br /> Well they could be defined as Community Defenders or they could be a manifestation of &quot;University Secret Societies&quot;. Perhaps they're both at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T08:09:38-08:00","id":797353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=797350#post797350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually that's what I was thinking of when I made the comparason. I mean, The Union might be written with xenophobia as their flaw - but in 2E talks about regional differences that doesn't have to apply to every location. In fact it would kind of miss the point if it did.<br /> <br /> Like the Union your proposed group are community defenders and they support individual cells regardless of how they choose to go about the hunt; supporting individual cells like that is the core of the Union.<br /> <br /> You bring up Night Watch, and Maiden's Blood Sisterhood. And well, why not? Lets call the archetype &quot;Community Defenders&quot;. Why not say that The Union are the Community Defenders of a largish wash of rust belt and small town USA. Night Watch are the community defenders of west side and east side Baltimore. Your group are the Community Defenders of various gay neighbourhoods. The Maiden's Blood Sisterhood...<br /> <br /> Well they could be defined as Community Defenders or they could be a manifestation of &quot;University Secret Societies&quot;. Perhaps they're both at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's a useful comparison to make, because it devalues the rich differences between those groups and further stymies other groups from tapping into it. I think Community Defenders is where the heart of Hunter is at, and they are applicable pretty much everywhere and fit a ridiculously diverse amount of character concepts.<br /> <br /> In a way, Community Defenders is the &quot;theme&quot; that hews closest to Hunter's metaphysical purpose, if we reference the &quot;origin story&quot; of HtV about the first mortals who glimpsed into the dark and chose to hold a candle against it. To me, that's where Hunter really shines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T08:17:57-08:00","id":797356,"title":"","content":"You're welcome to that opinion, but I disagree.<br /> <br /> Firstly I don't think it devalues the differences between those groups. If anything the enormous differences between those groups is exactly what is needed to show how Hunter is global with similar ideas being vastly different in different parts of the world. Even when those different parts are just different parts of America.<br /> <br /> <br /> Secondly I don't think Community Defenders is where the heart of Hunter is.<br /> <br /> There's 20 cannon compacts so far.<br /> There are only 2 who'd I'd call Community Defenders: Night Watch &amp; The Union<br /> <br /> If you stretch it you could include Ahl al-Jabal &amp; The Long Night but I'd call them &quot;Faith Based Hunters&quot;. You could also use Maiden's Blood Sisterhood, but like I said I'm leaning towards them being &quot;University Secret Society&quot;.<br /> <br /> But with all 5 it's still it's only a minority.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't like the idea of Hunter having a heart. The diveristy of the setting is it's appeal to me, so defining Community Defenders or anything as the heart rubs me the wrong way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T08:31:42-08:00","id":797359,"title":"","content":"I agree that Hunter's diversity is a great plus, but what I mean by &quot;the heart&quot; is &quot;where the emotional resonance is the highest.&quot; I think that out of all the different groups, it's Community Defenders that have the Hunter's relationships, emotions and affections on the line the most. While all forms of the Vigil are personal, it's those groups that tap into the character's social and emotional motivations. Most characters have loved ones. Many mortals, when faced with the reality that the world contains dangerous supernatural creatures, will want to protect their loved ones, and some will also want to protect innocent strangers out of a sense of empathy. Community Defenders tap into that network of empathy, affection and duty that is often overlooked because of its understatedness.<br /> <br /> I would also argue against the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood being purely academics or occultists. They have an entire subfaction dedicated to actually fighting supernatural horrors, the Amazons. While the book does state that it doesn't mean they're all trained warriors, it <i>does</i> emphasise that the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood are not helpless or lacking in the fighting department. They can take care of themselves with stake and gun just like any other Hunter group. Not to mention that the book also states they're no longer University-based, having expanded to soup kitchens, women's shelters and the like. They're Community Defenders through and through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T08:39:21-08:00","id":797366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=797359#post797359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that out of all the different groups, it's Community Defenders that have the Hunter's relationships, emotions and affections on the line the most. &quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not sure it is actually.<br /> <br /> I mean, I would think that family is the core relationship and affections that a Hunter puts on the line; every Compact has family. A Community Defender's link to his neighbours is more comparable to a Null Mysteriis or Barrett Comission's link to their co-workers.<br /> <br /> But this is mostly personal opinion and what's important in our real life social networks rather than something with an actual answer we can debate about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=797359#post797359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also argue against the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood being purely academics or occultists.</div> </div> </div> </div> I see nothing incompatible between &quot;know how to fight&quot; and &quot;university secret society&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T08:51:38-08:00","id":797372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=797366#post797366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not sure it is actually.<br /> <br /> I mean, I would think that family is the core relationship and affections that a Hunter puts on the line; every Compact has family. A Community Defender's link to his neighbours is more comparable to a Null Mysteriis or Barrett Comission's link to their co-workers.<br /> <br /> But this is mostly personal opinion and what's important in our real life social networks rather than something with an actual answer we can debate about.<br /> <br /> I see nothing incompatible between &quot;know how to fight&quot; and &quot;university secret society&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Vigil takes its toll on relationships, this is repeated time after time in the various Hunter groups. If you're working for Cheiron, TFV or Null Mysteriis, you're fraying your relationships for things that aren't related to them, like money and supernatural grafts, patriotism or science. Community Defenders actively do their best to counter that social fraying and to turn a Hunter's relationships into a weapon against the darkness (the Union specifically states in the in-character blurb in C&amp;C that their weapons are the people).<br /> <br /> That said, I do agree that it's ultimately futile to debate something so abstract. Practically speaking, it's important to highlight the sheer amount of diversity and emotional resonance in the Community Defender archetype. I think there's definitely room for more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T09:07:09-08:00","id":797378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=797350#post797350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd actually say there's three themes. How we Hunt, Why we Hunt, and Who we Are.<br /> <br /> But not all Compacts Have all three.<br /> <br /> The Maiden's Blood Sisterhood for example has all three:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">How we hunt: Accademic investigation, diplomacy, perhaps a splash of occultism.<br /> Why we hunt: To protect the student community.<br /> Who we are: Feminists / Students and University staff</div><br /> But Null Mysteriis only really does Why We Hunt.<br /> Ashwood Abbey does Why we Hunt and Who we Are, but it doesn't do How we Hunt.<br /> The Talbot Group does Why we Hunt and How we Hunt, but not Who we are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you about the three. Do you think that possibly having an answer to all three for each Compact in the 2e would do well to cut through some of the arguments over semantics on these threads? Because it seems to me that the issues over ethics, globalization, and tiers, can be tied to the unequal handling of each Compact and Conspiracy in their original write-up. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T09:32:24-08:00","id":797390,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. Probably not.<br /> <br /> Take Null Mysteriis. I don't think that going into detail on Who They Hunt would be an improvement. I think the fact NM hunt/study just about everything works well.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I would say is that answering those three questions for every Compact is a good idea. But N/A remains a valid answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T19:22:28-08:00","id":798061,"title":"","content":"Choosing my three favorite Compacts is not an easy task, but the ones that I tend to mine the most story out of would probably be:<br /> <br /> The Union \u2013 I love the Union in part because they are one of the most straightforward organizations. A loose affiliation of cells that are focused on dealing with local supernatural problems. This creates great potential for exploring the human impact of supernatural phenomena. What does a neighborhood infested by ghosts and plagued by demonic possession look like? How does the corrosive influence of vampiric control manifest itself? The Union also challenges one of the fundamental conceits of the World of Darkness; that regular people \u201cjust don't want to know.\u201d While the written history of the Union ties it rather closely to the American labor movement, I've generally used the Union as a catch-all for a variety of locally-minded organizations. The Union also plays into what I like to call \u201ceconomic horror\u201d or \u201crest belt gothic.\u201d The desperation and horror of being trapped in your small town/neighborhood with the monsters you know are hiding there, making the Vigil into an act of defiance or even revolution.<br /> <br /> Null Mysteriis \u2013 This is one that I feel gets misplayed a lot. To say that Null Mysteriis \u201cdoesn't believe\u201d in the supernatural misses the point. Null Mysteriis simply refuses to shrug its shoulders and resign itself to accepting the supernatural as unknowable and unquantifiable. They want to <i>understand</i> the supernatural, to throw aside the fear that the unknown creates in us and put it in a box. If it doesn't fit, you <i>build a bigger box.</i> While yes there's going to be a lot of flailing in the dark and misapprehension, eventually you are going to start making meaningful discoveries about the way the World of Darkness ticks. Secrets that even the monsters may not know about themselves. Null Mysteriis also lends itself well to entertaining techno-babble, drawing from Warren Ellis' Planetary and Charles Stross' Laundry Files as a couple of my personal favorites.<br /> <br /> Network Zero \u2013 I'll admit up front that I'm a sucker for found footage and creepypastas. Network Zero fits into that niche exceptionally well. A compact that focuses on what can be seen whose horror comes from what cannot be seen; from what is happening just out of frame. They also have a somewhat sideways approach to the Vigil, which creates potential for novel, non-linear, and even non-violent hunter plots. Other hunters might criticize Network Zero for not taking a more active combat role, but I'd argue that Network Zero is actually fighting the more important war. By attacking the veil of ignorance that the supernatural conspires to pull over humanity they are chipping away at one of the monsters' most important foundations. Every victory in the war of information and propaganda is another skeptic convinced, another candle lit in the Vigil.<br /> <br /> As to globalization for the compacts I've mentioned.<br /> <br /> The Union is bit of a paradox where that is concerned. On the one hand the factors which lead to the necessity of the Union are going to crop up all over the world. Its a very human and universal sort of Compact. On the other hand its local emphasis makes it unlikely to have a truly global organization and reach. One solution I might propose is having a number of Union-esque groups in different countries with different names and localized agendas, but which operate under the loosely affiliated franchise of the Union for the sake of simplicity. One easy area to expand them into would be Latin America with its history of both labor movements and locally organized militias.<br /> <br /> Null Mysteriis I've always seen as a global Compact. In my chronicles they are based in France and have inroads into the scientific establishment that criss-cross international boundaries. During the Cold War there was an ideological schism between Western and Soviet scientists in the Compact, but even then the back channels stayed open and both sides remained committed to their core goal of illuminating the murk of the supernatural and casting aside its superstitions. Something I've yet to work with but which I think would be interesting is to discuss the role Null Mysteriis plays in shaping the Vigil globally. I like to imagine that Null Mysteriis would see educating hunters as part of its mandate. Not only sharing information on proven knowledge and techniques but also in steering hunters away from false positives and superstitious bias that could result in innocent casualties.<br /> <br /> Network Zero has already been discussed at some length as a global Compact. It thrives on the internet and generally ignores borders. What would be interesting is to explore its role both in countries that have significant internet penetration and those that don't. Iran actually has an incredible number of connected internet users and a surprisingly unregulated web. Coupled with Iran's booming independent film industry Network Zero could definitely find a foothold, however strange, in the Islamic Republic. On the other hand we can look at China, which has a large population and an ever-growing number of connected users but tight government controls on the internet. How the Network operates behind the Great Firewall could be interesting. The bring things back into the Network's grainy A/V past it could be rewarding to look at some areas of Eastern Europe or Subsaharan Africa where there is limited internet connectivity and bootleg VHS tapes are still a thing. Cells are going to be less closely connected to the rest of the Compact and are going to have to work harder to get their message out.<br /> <br /> As far as histories are concerned I tend not to be overly attached to the canon. The historical actions of previous cells and members of the various Compacts do tend to come up in my games, but not really as extensions of the written material in the books.<br /> <br /> If I were to suggest a possible new play style I think what I would go with would be \u201cengagement.\u201d A group that seeks to be proactive rather than reactive in its interactions with the supernatural. Hunters are the only group in the World of Darkness for whom crossover is the default mode of the game. Taken as a whole they interact more often and with more splats than any of those splats do individually. There is potential there for a Vigil that is focused less on conflict with the supernatural than with managing its impact on the mortal world. Brokering a peace between the vampires and the werewolves because the hunters know more about either of them than they do about each other. Allying with a changeling court to help the reintegration of newly escaped changelings into society. Creating safe houses for nomadic Promethean throngs where the effects of wasteland will be minimized. Obviously there is still the potential for conflict in these situations, but conflict of a different sort than just finding the monster and driving a stake through its heart. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T18:01:25-08:00","id":798519,"title":"","content":"Wow Caitiff. I've been putting off writing up my favorites because I want to go in-depth about it and don't have the free time for it right now. But you've perfectly expressed my exact thoughts on my three favorite Compacts. Bravo.<br /> <br /> Also, kindly get out of my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T22:21:24-08:00","id":799061,"title":"","content":"Ironically, I always thought that the Mexican autodefensas as the best example of The Union.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1072-theye1","name":"theye1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1072_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T13:27:46-08:00","id":799778,"title":"","content":"I'm really hoping Habibti Ma makes it into the new book. They're probably my favorite Compact in the entire game, and have the potential for some really heartwrenching stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T13:56:01-08:00","id":799786,"title":"","content":"Speaking of which, I could have sworn I read that the Compact's name was meant to be &quot;Habibti Ma'at&quot;, but an error crept in. Am I remembering this correctly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T09:14:33-08:00","id":800610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=799786#post799786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which, I could have sworn I read that the Compact's name was meant to be &quot;Habibti Ma'at&quot;, but an error crept in. Am I remembering this correctly?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I edited Mortal Remains, and this is the first I'm hearing of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T10:22:50-08:00","id":800630,"title":"","content":"I've just found out where I got it from. TvTropes' article on &quot;Hunter: The Vigil&quot; claims it as the &quot;Word of God&quot;. They don't give any sources, though. Still, thank you for responding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T08:40:17-08:00","id":801419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=800630#post800630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've just found out where I got it from. TvTropes' article on &quot;Hunter: The Vigil&quot; claims it as the &quot;Word of God&quot;. They don't give any sources, though. Still, thank you for responding.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T12:38:47-08:00","id":801557,"title":"","content":"My three favorite compacts:<br /> <br /> 1. Ashwood Abbey - I have always adored this compact, as the idea of a Hellfire Club hunting monsters for the fun of it has been ridiculously easy to incorporate into my games time after time. I like that they are a bit darker than some of the other compacts, and that they might make other hunters a bit uncomfortable. That's one of the reasons that I hope they don't end up as an antagonist faction in the new edition. I like the idea that this compact is made up of the allies that the other hunters aren't sure they really want, while finding it difficult to deny their usefulness.<br /> <br /> 2. Habibti Ma - Given how many of the various supernatural beings create cults, a group that focuses its efforts on helping the people that are taken in by them is a great touch for the setting. It also opens up the amusing plots of the hunters kidnapping an actual supernatural being in the mistaken belief that the new friends and strange behavior that their loved one is now displaying is the result of cult activity.<br /> <br /> 3. Network Zero - I have always felt that they were a great compact that are fairly easy to drop into most chronicles. Their focus on proving the existence of the supernatural makes for a threat that many supernatural beings may not be anticipating.<br /> <br /> I think that all three of these compacts could be globalized with ease. For Ashwood Abbey, all it takes is adding new chapters in whatever city you want. Network Zero I've always treated as globalized anyway, given that they are connected through the internet. Habibti Ma may be a little bit trickier, but cults are a problem all over the world, so it is natural that this group or similar ones could spring up anywhere. Of course, I've usually treated most of the compacts as global organizations in my games anyway, so perhaps I'm a bit biased.<br /> <br /> The histories of the compacts are interesting, but I often tweak them for my games as the needs of story demand anyway, so whatever little twists you add to the history to justify a more global presence would be fine with me.<br /> <br /> As for a new playing style, I like a lot of the ideas that others have suggested previously, and would have a difficult time deciding on just one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T15:39:58-08:00","id":801638,"title":"","content":"I would, quite honestly, prefer a hefty section on building a Compact from the ground up, with the &quot;canon&quot; Compacts acting as examples. I'm <i>much</i> more of a toolkit guy - there's a reason I'm not answering the question about what my favorite Compacts are (I've never actually bothered to read through them; heck, I only read the stuff on Conspiracies to pillage them for mechanics.)<br /> <br /> I know for a fact that I'll most likely end up ignoring any concretely written Compact in the new corebook, <i>regardless</i> of how well it's all written - however, a mini chapter on <i>designing</i> a Compact would essentially be design porn for me.<br /> <br /> (Also, I think you need to remember your 5 W's and your H when designing a Compact - though I'd say that the Who, What, Why, and How show up more often than the Where and When.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T15:54:45-08:00","id":801647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=801638#post801638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would, quite honestly, prefer a hefty section on building a Compact from the ground up, with the &quot;canon&quot; Compacts acting as examples. I'm <i>much</i> more of a toolkit guy - there's a reason I'm not answering the question about what my favorite Compacts are (I've never actually bothered to read through them; heck, I only read the stuff on Conspiracies to pillage them for mechanics.)<br /> <br /> I know for a fact that I'll most likely end up ignoring any concretely written Compact in the new corebook, <i>regardless</i> of how well it's all written - however, a mini chapter on <i>designing</i> a Compact would essentially be design porn for me.<br /> <br /> (Also, I think you need to remember your 5 W's and your H when designing a Compact - though I'd say that the Who, What, Why, and How show up more often than the Where and When.)</div> </div> </div> </div>While I am open to giving certain groups the benefit of the doubt if they wow me (such as my top 3), I have to wholeheartedly agree with this.<br /> <br /> Mirrors was by far my favourite book in the nWoD line because it gave me everything I wanted: Options. Tools. Menus. Levers to tinker and fiddle with. I would be so happy if the new editions had a more &quot;enable the storyteller to build their own stuff&quot; section in the core, or even a whole book on it, like Mirrors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T02:58:30-08:00","id":801900,"title":"","content":"\u2022 What are your top 3 favorite<br /> <br /> existing compacts and why? These can be pulled from any book that\u2019s been published thus far, including compacts that are no longer around.<br /> <br /> The Ashwood Abbey \u2013 Because I love playing a hedonistic anti-hero that will not only kill anything but also desecrate it with a devil may care grin. Also, without them I couldn\u2019t have Little Timmy, my favorite Hunter NPC. I can\u2019t think of an acceptable way for a Hunter, not a Slasher, to do a fist full of coke before taking what is clearly a two handed shotgun and jumping blindly into a Nosferatu catacomb as he screams, \u201cYEEEAAAHHH\u201d without a pause to remember what they did to his other hand yesterday.<br /> <br /> Network Zero \u2013 I know a lot of people enjoy playing this group because of their \u201cTruth seeking\u201d but personally, I just like them because I enjoy an underdog who\u2019s desperate to make the world all make sense, which isn\u2019t to say kill, capture, or understand it and while that could be true of any compact, there\u2019s a certain level of isolation with the Network since they\u2019re primarily an online assistance kind of group. No Hunter compact can suspend disbelief like they can as far as walking blindly into the darkness unprepared, not to mention, as NPC\u2019s they can make or break a tier 1 game anywhere anytime as talking heads.<br /> <br /> (None) \u2013 I could say the Union, Talbot Group or Utopia Now for various reasons but these would just be aesthetic reasons that I flip back and forth through while running/playing. Honestly the rest have never settled well to me. You\u2019d think that with experience more Hunters would intermingle a bit more with the Splats that don\u2019t inherently want to kill them, maybe even learn something legitimate about the larger world as a whole, but they don\u2019t. Every single compact at this level has very large misgivings and even though they have the resources and capacity to see and know something about the other Splats they just don\u2019t seem to care to do more than shoot them to death, despite the fact that it\u2019s contrary to their ethos. I think Tier 2 should definitely see more cooperation with the other splats.<br /> <br /> Oh, and an Honorable Nod to, Precinct 13. Which I adapted into a compact out of the tales from Precinct 13 resource book.<br /> <br /> \u2022 What are your thoughts on globalization and locations for the compacts you selected?<br /> <br /> I think it only makes sense that they have globalization. To be fair though, that\u2019s how I\u2019ve always ran my HtV games. I usually use the 2nd tier compacts that are in all of my major cities as a platform to learn about the various Splats that are specific to a region. Otherwise you just get the same old \u201cSlay the Dragon\u201d/ \u201cSave the Princess\u201d plot lines over and over again with really flat and boring antagonist that no one can really sympathize.<br /> <br /> Though I would like to offer you an alternative that may have already occurred to you:<br /> What if a \u201cCompact\u201d was more of an archetypical philosophy than an organization per say. Meaning that \u201cThe Union\u201d is simply a term for any Worker\u2019s Union or Parent Teacher Association or etc. that wants to keep their kids safe from the thing that has plagued their community for a time. That way it\u2019s more like an auspice or a path than a literal organization, though they could have one. It\u2019d make a lot of sense in the communication age for these like-minded hunters to band together.<br /> <br /> \u2022 How married are you to the history of the compacts? Have those details come up in actual play for your group?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not, there\u2019s always a better way to spin an idea and holding ideologies on a pedestal is what has caused most of the problems in our world when it comes to organized society so, I trust you, and if you fail there\u2019s always 3rd Ed. Also the histories have come up in game but, to be fair, when you guys write 80,000 \u2013 200,000 or more words about a gameline that I enjoy, I\u2019m gonna use reference material at any given opportunity, as a writer I feel like adding depth to a gameline can never be a bad thing, perhaps not corebook material but never a bad thing. Personally I\u2019d do small PDF\u2019s between releases at drive thru and sell them individually as their released \u201cdigital only\u201d and then offer print on demand for the compendium once there\u2019s 12 or so.<br /> <br /> \u2022 We have compacts formed around playing styles such as belief, hedonism, research, atonement, communication, defense, vengeance, hunting specific monster types such as vampires, etc. If you had your pick of \u201ca\u201d new style of play that\u2019d be fun to play, what would be the theme and why? Where would it be based? Please try to avoid creating/naming new compacts, as I do want to reserve that honor for my future team. <br /> <br /> Well, I\u2019d say \u201cRefinement\u201d of the compact in the adversity of the World of Darkness.<br /> Westering (if you get the reference) from Steinbach\u2019s, Leader of the People. Steinbach used the term Westering to refer to the communal nature of immigrants who were moving west during the gold rush and how the harsh life of travel in a caravan brought the best out of them as whole.<br /> <br /> Not to give a specific style but rather finding strength through a refinement of different ideals in a close knit community.<br /> <br /> A creed of \u201cstrength in diversity\u201d which is to say that each Hunter would have their own unique code and skill set to bring to the table. <br /> <br /> Example community: Carnival Workers, Southern Aristocrats, Late-Night Clerks, Janitorial Service, a Close knit community is the easy choice such as a Chinatown or Spiritual Congregation, and really just any exceptional hunter cell that empathizes (not to say sympathizes) with the Splats that they come across in the Vigil without inherently burning them at the stake.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6516-mefathiel8","name":"mefathiel8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T11:42:40-08:00","id":803233,"title":"","content":"so I assume there is no open dev post this week. Oh well...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:28:05-08:00","id":803265,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#555555\">What are your top 3 favorite existing compacts and why? These can be pulled from any book that\u2019s been published thus far, including compacts that are no longer around.</span><br /> <br /> Null Mysteriis: This compact is uniquely setting agnostic, they don't accept the basic conceit that the supernatural is unnatural or unexplainable. As a Storyteller it forced me to broaden the scope of the game and inspired several &quot;weird science&quot; sessions. It rewards players for being clever (I'm Doing Science in particular) and thinking about the setting in a different light.<br /> <br /> Network Zero: It brought Hunter the Vigil into its own and kept it from being &quot;Year of the Hunter&quot; the core book by showing how the otherworldly isn't immune information technology. The Compact is a perfect tool for dropping leads onto players and is broad enough to encompass all manner of play styles.<br /> <br /> Heritage House: For those unfamiliar with Glimpses of the Unknown this Compact believes hunters should cooperate and train their children to be hunters. This explores the hunt from the perspective of a family. There's also no barrier to new players or expectations, its simplicity and relatability is its strength. For Storytellers it\u2019s a Compact explicitly designed to play well with others, built up by players, or used as antagonists (like the compound in the SAS Bad Night at Blackmoon Farm).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\">What are your thoughts on globalization and locations for the compacts you selected?</span><br /> <br /> I think it will be a fine line to walk with each compact as being an amalgam of a culture, philosophy, and methodology or<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797033-open-dev-two-compacts-and-globalization?p=797350#post797350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How we Hunt, Why we Hunt, and Who we Are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would look to how real world communities and organizations have spread or changed. Developers should design 'splinter' or offshoot Compacts, because communities redefine themselves constantly. As long as they're an interesting take with a different flavor rather than a stereotyped or generalized Compact.<br /> <br /> With Null Mysteriis 2nd ed. should globalize their initiatives. A global roster of members with a rotating annual convention or congress to discuss the year's focus and praise distinguished members. I had this very thing happen in Boston, noting the next was to occur in Cairn, Australia. It gave my player a chance to mingle and politic as well as opening the door for a fish out of water story. I'd focus on funding drives or big projects. Maybe there's a team trying to mount an expedition to the Antarctic to discover what's been released by the melting of the ice shelves or in the Maldives to learn what they can before they are gone.<br /> <br /> Network Zero from the previews is globalized in membership because of the ease of access. It could follow piracy or anonymous style communities, having additional hubs in the Netherlands, Latvia, and Romania but I think what is of more interest is this Compact exists independent of a physical place. They can launch coordinated online assaults, set up meetups and flashmobs, and vie for status all from a cellphone. And what horrors lurk online? Darknet monsters, banned former Network Zero Slashers, compromised hunter communities?<br /> <br /> Heritage House is brand new. I don't think it needs to be globalized, because it is built off a collection of families, trying to make it larger would detract from the intimacy of the organization. I would put the compound near Vancouver, Portland, or Kansas somewhere wooded and secluded focused more on training and family dynamics. The book might even not lock it down, providing a few 'rumors' about where this Compact began and operates. Hunters themselves could be found offering aid to hunters all over the world or every House member upon reaching 'hunter' status might be tasked with going out and finding a cell to join in support of their mission to unify hunters.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\">How married are you to the history of the compacts? Have those details come up in actual play for your group?</span><br /> <br /> For myself the history of a compact is only as relevant as its best story hook. One of my player's character is from Heritage House and a second generation hunter raised by the Compact, I moved the timeline forward. But I really enjoyed the way Vampire 2nd muddied the origin stories of the clans and I think Hunter should do something similar. It would be interesting not to limit a Compacts to such a short (compared to Conspiracies) history, they could claim to descend from an older organization (even if they aren't).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\">We have compacts formed around playing styles such as belief, hedonism, research, atonement, communication, defense, vengeance, hunting specific monster types such as vampires, etc. If you had your pick of \u201ca\u201d new style of play that\u2019d be fun to play, what would be the theme and why? Where would it be based? Please try to avoid creating/naming new compacts, as I do want to reserve that honor for my future team</span><br /> <br /> I think one of the things that made Hunter the Reckoning work was that it was upfront about how and what you were going to play. Being a Martyr is right there in the name. I think Hunter the Vigil 2nd should strive to be as explicit with the themes of all the Compacts.<br /> <br /> A new Compact would be formed around &quot;Law.&quot; Society determines who is accepted or rejected, humane or monstrous, and right or wrong. In the Chronicles of Darkness society has collectively turned a blind eye to the supernatural. Monsters are allowed to parasitize civilization because they have always been here. Hunters turn defy laws to deal with what society will not. In doing so they act as the monsters act, above law and order.<br /> <br /> The focus of such a Compact is on doing what can be done through negotiation and promises. Corruption has given us the world we have and compromise is preferable to cycles of violence and war. It would be born from the 'kidnap and ransom' industry of Latin America. Given their contact with secret (criminal) societies a charismatic negotiator might have &quot;struck a deal with the devil&quot;. Mexico City would be a good central location given the negotiation culture, mythology, and its government's failure to stop drug cartels and human trafficking. This 'company' or 'cartel' could have offices in Argentina, Los Angeles, Tijuana, Morocco, and Madrid. It would be willing to do barter with evil to contain it. Maybe every member has a 'black book' of blackmail and a 'red book' of names of more violent hunters. In game it would facilitate coalitions of hunters working toward a common end (see: a group of players). Your negotiators see a monster civil war brewing or are even contacted by monsters to get other hunters off their back.<br /> <br /> Inspiration for this sort of game would be shows like the Shield. Vic Mackey strikes deals with bad people to do 'good' and 'take care' of his people something that his ineffective, overly bureaucratic, and corrupt police department can't seem to manage. With creatures like vampires, changelings, demons, and mages able to magically enforce deals these would naturally tie in with these monsters. Tense battles of wills with monster contracts or midnight meetings to bring to former enemies to a table.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1783-spanishinquisition","name":"SpanishInquisition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T21:04:19-08:00","id":820130,"title":"","content":"So this article may be interesting in the context of Global Hunters:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://news.nationalgeographic.com/2016/01/160128-zanzibar-herbalist-jinni-exorcist/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://assets-cdn.nationalgeographic.com/natgeo/static/default.NG.logo.dark.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://news.nationalgeographic.com/2016/01/160128-zanzibar-herbalist-jinni-exorcist/\" target=\"_blank\"> National Geographic </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://news.nationalgeographic.com/2016/01/160128-zanzibar-herbalist-jinni-exorcist/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://news.nationalgeographic.com/2016/01/160128-zanzibar-herbalist-jinni-exorcist/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Explore National Geographic. A world leader in geography, cartography and exploration. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I have no idea what Said's Faith is like, but I can totally see Ahl Al-Jabal who are like him: Muslim Hunters who only use violence against monsters as a last resort, preferring faith and diplomacy. It just reinforces my desire to see them as one of the core compacts. Plus, Said's description of Jinn sound a lot like CofD's spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}